# Private and special-use address space (RFC 1918, 5735, 5737, 6598, 4193, 4291).
# These prefixes do not change, so they are pinned here rather than fetched.
#
# The lan ruleset sets no_resolve, which applies to IP rules only. That matters
# because lan is the first ruleset in every profile: without no-resolve, the very
# first rule a domain request meets would force a DNS lookup.
#
# 198.18.0.0/15 is deliberately absent. Every supported client uses it as its
# fake-IP range, and claiming it here would collide with that machinery.

# IPv4
0.0.0.0/8
10.0.0.0/8
100.64.0.0/10
127.0.0.0/8
169.254.0.0/16
172.16.0.0/12
192.0.0.0/24
192.0.2.0/24
192.88.99.0/24
192.168.0.0/16
198.51.100.0/24
203.0.113.0/24
224.0.0.0/4
255.255.255.255/32

# IPv6
::1/128
fc00::/7
fe80::/10
ff00::/8

# Additional local or private domains can be added below.
